    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0698" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg574"/>

                <head>No. 347.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Sir Edward
                        Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 4,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my reply of the 17th ultimo,
                    to your note of the 23d of November last, in relation to an alleged attack by
                    Indians from the United States upon a party of Stony Indians of Canada, I now
                    have the honor to inform you that I have received a letter from my colleague,
                    the Secretary of the Interior, dated the 28th ultimo, in which he says that an
                    investigation has been ordered by the Indian Office, with a view to the
                    discovery and punishment of those who may be found guilty of the outrage in
                    question.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
